# Player-facing copy

Before writing or editing player-facing copy (stories, Story Library banks, insights, Focus, trait descriptions, legends, buttons, tooltips, empty states, onboarding, notifications), read `docs/voice-guide.md` and follow it.

Meaning first (emci, 2026-10-23). This replaces "show every trait through a real moment." Say what the line means. Do not invent the player's history. Do not refer to a thing that is not on screen. Match the purpose: a button names the action, an error says what happened and what to do, an insight says what the answers suggest, a comparison states the real similarity or difference. A story may use a scene. Other screens should not all sound like a story card. Humor is optional. Cut it when it makes the line less accurate.

`npm run check:player-copy` and `npm run check:story-library` must pass. They refuse the coach phrases in the voice guide (including "energy") and slang outside the casual tier. They do not require a scene phrase, a flip scene, a joke, a ban on ticket / kettle / fork / bag / chair / costume, or one sentence shape per card. That shape cap pushed a false "when". They do flag an opener used by more than about a third of a pool, and a legend fact repeated on one card. Prefer a true connection. Vary the opening. "You'd rather" must not start most lines. A hypothetical hour with a legend opens "Picture an hour with…". Reserved is "You recharge with time to yourself."

Slots are only names, pronouns, `{deed}` (a sourced clause), and the player's own answer. Each line has eligibility and a priority. The highest eligible line wins, and a shown line does not repeat until that pool is used up. Keep trait ids, data meaning, and `STORY_LIBRARY_RUNTIME` (it ships off).

Do not invent or redefine traits. If the meaning of a line is uncertain, flag it. Do not guess a new meaning.
